Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 22:07:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: remove hosted services and telemetry

X-Jcode-Patch-Intent: Strip hosted services, telemetry, promotional
content, onboarding, and sponsored integrations from jcode
X-Jcode-Patch-Kind: personal-feature
X-Jcode-Patch-Depends-On: 1005-personal-provider-add-typed-openrouter-eu-provider.patch

Patch intent:
Remove all hosted/cloud service features: subscription and billing
commands, account CLI and TUI commands, promotional and onboarding
content, sponsored integration discovery, telemetry delivery, and
the hosted subscription account API. Route the jcode provider choice
through direct endpoint configuration instead of the managed
subscription wrapper. Remove associated documentation.

Why it exists:
The personal jcode build operates without hosted accounts, tiers,
billing, telemetry, or sponsored content. These features are removed
to keep the build local-only and free of promotional or cloud-service
code paths.

Upstream integration points:
crates/jcode-tui/src/tui/app.rs, crates/jcode-tui/src/tui/app/
onboarding_flow.rs, crates/jcode-app-core/src/tool/discover.rs,
src/cli/account.rs, src/cli/provider_init.rs, crates/jcode-base/
src/lib.rs, TELEMETRY.md, README.md, docs/

Update guidance:
Keep all hosted service, telemetry, promotional, and onboarding code
paths removed. The jcode provider choice must use the generic
OpenAI-compatible profile, not the managed subscription wrapper. Do
not reintroduce subscription runtime activation, managed account
credentials, telemetry delivery, or sponsored integration discovery.

Validation:
scripts/cargo_exec.sh check -p jcode
scripts/cargo_exec.sh test -p jcode jcode_choice_uses_the_generic_direct_endpoint_profile --lib
